Suite: Kettle

# One kettle app, built three times. Plain lines are about every one of them; a [tag] says
# how one differs. Each app embeds the Expectation driver for its stack.

Vocabulary:
  Platform: GPUI | SwiftUI | React Native

  State: the kettle is off | starting | heating | dry
    Shows: off: the display reads OFF
    Shows: heating: the display reads HEATING and the light turns red
    Shows: dry: the display reads DRY
  State: the dial is 0..100 %
    Set: drag the DIAL slider to {value}
  State: the preset is WARM | HOT | BOIL
    Shows: the PRESET line reads {value}
  State: the child lock is on | off
    Shows: on: the LOCK badge lights up
    Shows: off: the LOCK badge goes dark

  Event: the user presses start
    Say: click START
    Say[SwiftUI]: tap START
    Say[React Native]: tap START
  Event: the user presses reset
    Say: click RESET
    Say[SwiftUI]: tap RESET
    Say[React Native]: tap RESET
  Event: the user presses preset
    Say: click PRESET
    Say[SwiftUI]: tap PRESET
    Say[React Native]: tap PRESET
  Event: the user presses lock
    Say: click LOCK
    Say[SwiftUI]: tap LOCK
    Say[React Native]: tap LOCK
  Event: the water runs out

  Phrase: the kettle is plugged in and full
    Say: open the app
    Given the kettle is off
    And the dial is 0 %
    And the preset is WARM
    And the child lock is off

Background:
  Given the kettle is plugged in and full

Term: display
  The panel at the top of the app. It shows the preset, the state and the water temperature.
